23. Sniffing kya hai? ⭐

Sniffing = Network traffic ko capture aur analyze karna.

Network mein packets travel karte hain. Sniffing tools in packets ko capture karke traffic ko analyze kar sakte hain.

24. Packet

Network par data usually small units mein travel karta hai jise packets kehte hain.

Packet mein information ho sakti hai:

Source
Destination
Protocol
Ports
Payload/data
25. Passive Sniffing ⭐

Passive sniffing mein attacker/network observer traffic ko capture karta hai without actively modifying network traffic.

Example environment:

Shared/broadcast-style network traffic monitoring.

Keyword:

Passive = Listen

26. Active Sniffing ⭐

Active sniffing mein attacker network traffic ko capture karne ke liye network environment ko actively influence/manipulate karne ki attempt karta hai.

Common concept:

ARP poisoning

Keyword:

Active = Manipulate + Capture

27. ARP

ARP = Address Resolution Protocol

Local network mein IP address ko corresponding MAC address se map karne ke liye use hota hai.

Example:

IP → MAC

28. ARP Poisoning

ARP poisoning mein attacker forged ARP information ke through devices ko incorrect IP-to-MAC mapping believe karwane ki attempt karta hai.

Potential result:

Traffic attacker ke system ki taraf redirect ho sakta hai.

Ye Man-in-the-Middle (MITM) situation create karne mein use ho sakta hai.

29. MAC Flooding

MAC flooding attack mein attacker switch ke MAC address table ko excessive/forged MAC entries se overwhelm karne ki attempt karta hai.

Agar switch properly handle na kare, to traffic handling behavior change ho sakta hai.

30. Sniffing se kya information expose ho sakti hai?

Agar communication properly encrypted nahi hai, network traffic se potentially:

Usernames
Passwords
Messages
Cookies
Session information
Other sensitive data

expose ho sakta hai.

Isliye HTTPS/TLS aur encrypted protocols important hain.
